# UI-MINIMAP-2: the stepped zoom (--zoom-mode stepped, the original's three groups) keeps the
# original's magnifier clamp to levels 0..2 (AnnoFrame 0x10007710, 0x10007692; docs/re/ui.md
# 2.9), although zoom.min_tile (zoom_floor over this mode's levels, thousandths of a pixel: with
# no derived levels, level 2 / sqrt 2) lies past level 2: the - stops at level 2, the + at level
# 0. The continuous zoom's extra stages: ui_magnifier_range.
# Launch (--gpu, so that --zoom-mode stepped itself, not the CPU renderer, picks the stepped
# zoom): --play data/maps/lan5.txt --construction-menu on --layout data/ui --zoom-mode stepped
resize 1024 768
wait frames 5
look 1140 516
wait frames 5
expect fact view.tile_w == 20
expect fact zoom.min_tile < 20000
expect fact zoom.at_min == 0
# The magnifier's - (826, 153), 19 x 21, at level 2: nothing changes.
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact view.tile_w == 20
expect fact zoom.at_min == 0
# The + (796, 135): one group per press (a group still being built applies when ready), clamped
# at level 0.
click_px 805 145
wait fact view.tile_w == 42
click_px 805 145
wait fact view.tile_w == 84
click_px 805 145
wait frames 3
expect fact view.tile_w == 84
# And back down to level 2, where the - stops again.
click_px 835 163
wait fact view.tile_w == 42
click_px 835 163
wait fact view.tile_w == 20
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact view.tile_w == 20
expect fact zoom.at_min == 0
expect fact selection.clicks == 0
expect fact camera.pans == 0
quit
